+# The contract the first log pass failed on
+
+Status: ready-for-agent
+
+Blocked by: nothing. 05 ran the pass; this is what the pass found, and 05 cannot
+reach the bar until it lands.
+
+**Read first**: `evals/logger/charter.md` (the seam -- and the two lines below
+that this ticket does not move), `docs/logging/eval-set.md` § *How to read a
+row* and § *What the runner has to set up*, CONTEXT.md § *adherence* and
+§ *provenance*, ADR-0004.
+
+The first pass of `trainer eval --suite log` against the graph held **24 of 90**
+on `gpt-oss:20b`. Rescored by hand on the document the engine would write, the
+50 determined runs that produced a document go from **7 to 30** held. The model
+is mostly reading the sentence correctly; what fails is the contract between the
+shape, the prompt and the scorer.
+
+| # | the fault | where |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | every value in a block is required, so a number the user never gave has to be written and labelled -- the prompt forbids `assumed`, the set expects it | `log.PerformedItem`, `log.PerformedBlock`, `logger.LOGGING` |
+| 2 | the exclusion vocabulary is nowhere in the context, so the value is a guess, and a guess `classify` does not know is refused -- which ends the run | `logger.LOGGING`, `logger.brief` |
+| 3 | the document is compared before adherence, so a value the engine fills in is scored against one the model was forced to write | `log_evaluation._difference` |
+
+## What to build
+
+### 1. A value nobody gave is left out
+
+`tools.strict_schema` makes every property required, so `amount`, `rounds` and
+`rest` -- and their three provenances -- have to carry something. A report of
+*"solo 2 serie"* says nothing about the reps or the rest, and the model's only
+options are to copy the prescription and call it `reported`, which is a lie
+about what the user said, or to call it `assumed`, which the prompt forbids and
+the charter reserves for code. U2, U3, U4, U13 and U14 all turn on it.
+
+- **Nullable, in pairs**: `amount`/`amount_source`, `rounds`/`rounds_source`,
+  `rest`/`rest_source`, each written together or both null -- the rule
+  `load_kg` already has, and the same model validator shape.
+- **Every bound stays** where the value is present: `amount >= 1`,
+  `rounds >= 1`, `rest >= 0`, provenance one of the three.
+- **`to_performed` fills a null** from the prescribed block `_paired` matched,
+  marked `assumed` -- the fill it already does for an item the document never
+  names, now reaching a value inside a block the document does name.
+- **`validate` reads the nulls**: a null in a block that pairs with nothing
+  prescribed has nothing to be filled from, and is refused by the sentence
+  `_nothing_assumed_without_a_prescription` already says -- there is no
+  prescription to have assumed it from. See *What is not built*, line 2: this
+  is why U6 is still expected to fail.
+- **The prompt says how**, in the bullet that already says a value nobody gave
+  is left out: leave it out by writing `null` for the value and its provenance.
+  The `assumed` paragraph goes -- the model can no longer be in a position to
+  need it.
+
+### 2. The exclusion vocabulary is read from the data
+
+`classify` accepts a `movement_pattern` or a `loaded_joints` value, character
+for character, and the model is shown two examples and nothing else. It is the
+project's standing rule in the one place it was never applied: vocabulary that
+exists in the data is read from the data.
+
+- `catalog.values(connection, "movement_pattern")` and
+  `catalog.joint_values(connection)`, in the system prompt's exclusion section.
+- **Read when the run opens**, not when the graph is built: the bot builds once
+  at startup, and `trainer db import` after that would leave a vocabulary the
+  catalog no longer has.
+- The model still decides whether the report is about pain at all and which
+  term it names; nothing in the list says which to pick, and the granularity
+  stays `classify`'s.
+
+### 3. Scored on the document the engine would write
+
+`_difference` compares the emitted blocks to the row's expected blocks by
+equality. The set writes its expected documents with the filled-in values
+spelled out (`rest: 150, rest_source: "assumed"`), which after item 1 is no
+longer what a correct agent emits.
+
+- **Resolve both sides** with `log.to_performed` and compare those -- the same
+  move the volume check already makes, and for the same reason the set gives
+  for scoring volume over the resolved workout. The rows do not change: they
+  declare the same facts, compared in the form that reaches the database.
+- **`workout_id`, `report` and `proposed_exclusion` stay on the document**:
+  adherence does not touch them.
+- **Keep the set's *only the deviations are written* rule as its own failure.**
+  Equality on raw blocks was enforcing it by accident, and on the resolved
+  document a restated prescription and an empty document are the same thing. A
+  determined row whose emitted block claims nothing of its own -- no value
+  `reported` or `asked`, which is `_CLAIMED` and `_filled` already -- fails
+  under `DOCUMENT`, naming the block. U1's note calls restating the commonest
+  wrong answer there is, and it stays caught.
+
+### 4. The pass, again
+
+- `trainer eval --suite log` against ollama `gpt-oss:20b`, the number written
+  into this ticket beside the 24 of 90, with the drop reported per row.
+- **`TRAINER_DB` names the fixture**: `prepared` does it, and nothing the agent
+  reads is visible to it otherwise.
+- The free checks first -- the suite, mypy, `log_evaluation.verify`, which
+  recomputes every expected volume against the new `to_performed` and is the
+  thing that says item 1 did not quietly change what a row costs.
+
+## What is not built
+
+Two lines in `evals/logger/charter.md`. Neither is moved here, and neither is
+written into the charter.
+
+1. **A refusal ends the run** (charter, *Constrained*: *one emission call, and a
+   refused document ends the run -- the planner replans; this does not*). One
+   bad field costs the whole row, including the deviation the model read
+   correctly: a wrong exclusion value loses the training it was reported
+   alongside. Sending the refusal back to the model, the way the planner's goes
+   back, would buy those rows. Item 2 removes the commonest cause of the
+   refusal, which is the part that can be built without the line.
+2. **`assumed` is never the model's** (charter, *Constrained*). Where a block
+   pairs with nothing prescribed -- a substitution, U6 -- nobody can fill the
+   value: code has no prescribed counterpart to read it from, and which
+   prescribed exercise a substitute stands in for is a judgement the engine
+   does not make. The set expects `rest: 150, "assumed"` there, and
+   `log._nothing_assumed_the_prescription_does_not_say` documents `assumed` as
+   the honest label in exactly that case. So the set, the validator's own
+   reasoning and the charter disagree about one cell, and U6 cannot be held by
+   any agent until that is settled. Letting the model write `assumed` **only**
+   where the prescription is silent would buy it.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- [ ] A hand-written document with `amount`, `rounds` and `rest` all null,
+      through `trainer log --from FILE` against a prescribed workout, renders
+      the prescribed numbers marked `(assumed)` -- watched, not read.
+- [ ] The same document with no `workout_id` is refused, naming the values that
+      have no prescription behind them.
+- [ ] A run of the logger proposing an exclusion shows the catalog's own
+      vocabulary in the prompt it was given -- read off the run record, not off
+      the source.
+- [ ] `trainer eval --suite log` has been **run** on ollama `gpt-oss:20b`, and
+      the number is written in this ticket against the 24 of 90, with the drop
+      per row.
+- [ ] In that pass, **no determined row fails** on a provenance difference for a
+      value its report never mentions, and **none** on an exclusion value
+      `classify` refuses. A row that fails because the model read the sentence
+      wrong is a reading failure and stays.
+- [ ] `log_evaluation.verify` reports no problems: every expected volume in the
+      set still costs what the set says it does.
+- [ ] The full test suite and mypy are green.
+
+## Comments
+
+Paid calls: the pass above is ollama and local, so it is free. A second pass on
+Groq is the one that costs, and it is not in the criteria -- 05 is where *on
+both providers* is asked for. Agree a budget with the user before it runs.
